{%- set faqs = [
  ["What are DevSecOps services?", "DevSecOps services integrate security practices into the software development lifecycle by combining automated security testing and vulnerability management with development and operations workflows. These services help identify security risks early and support secure software delivery."],
  ["Why are DevSecOps services important for businesses?", "DevSecOps services help businesses detect vulnerabilities before deployment and reduce the cost of fixing security issues later. They also improve security visibility and support faster software releases through automated security checks."],
  ["What does a DevSecOps company do?", "A DevSecOps company integrates security tools and processes into development pipelines and cloud infrastructure. Services commonly include CI/CD pipeline security and application security testing alongside container security and continuous vulnerability monitoring."],
  ["Which security tools are used in DevSecOps?", "DevSecOps tools include SAST and DAST scanners alongside Software Composition Analysis (SCA) platforms and container image scanners. Infrastructure as Code security tools and secrets detection solutions also help identify configuration weaknesses and exposed credentials."],
  ["How does DevSecOps improve CI/CD pipeline security?", "DevSecOps improves CI/CD pipeline security by integrating automated security checks into build and deployment stages. These checks can detect vulnerable dependencies and insecure code while identifying exposed secrets before software reaches production."],
  ["What is the difference between DevSecOps and traditional security testing?", "Traditional security testing often takes place at specific stages of development or before release. DevSecOps integrates security checks throughout the development lifecycle so teams can identify and address vulnerabilities continuously."],
  ["Can DevSecOps secure cloud infrastructure?", "Yes. DevSecOps integrates cloud security checks into infrastructure provisioning and deployment workflows. These checks help identify misconfigurations and excessive permissions across AWS and Azure environments while improving Infrastructure as Code security."],
  ["How does DevSecOps support container and Kubernetes security?", "DevSecOps integrates container image scanning and Kubernetes configuration reviews into deployment pipelines. These controls help detect vulnerable packages and insecure settings before containerized applications are deployed."],
  ["Does DevSecOps help with compliance requirements?", "DevSecOps can support compliance by integrating security policies and automated validation into development workflows. Depending on the organization's requirements, these controls can help demonstrate alignment with frameworks such as ISO 27001 and SOC 2."],
  ["How long does DevSecOps implementation take?", "The implementation timeline depends on application complexity and the existing development infrastructure alongside the number of pipelines and security tools involved. A focused implementation may take a few weeks while larger enterprise environments can require several months."],
  ["How can CipherTrivia help with DevSecOps implementation?", "CipherTrivia helps organizations strengthen software security through DevSecOps assessments and automated security testing alongside CI/CD pipeline reviews and vulnerability remediation guidance. Our services focus on identifying security gaps and integrating practical security controls across the software development lifecycle."]
] %}

